  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Cooking a perfect steak at home shows confidence and skill that translates well in dating contexts. Understanding the fundamentals of steak preparation eliminates guesswork and ensures consistent, restaurant-quality results. For date night, mastering this technique demonstrates capability and attention to detail."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "icon": "📖",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**In this guide:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "How to choose the right steak",
        "Essential preparation steps",
        "Cooking methods for perfect results",
        "How to tell when it's done"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Choosing Your Steak"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Best Cuts for Date Night"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Ribeye**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Marbling: Excellent (most flavorful)",
        "Tenderness: Very tender",
        "Thickness: 1.5 inches ideal",
        "Why: Forgiving due to high fat content, hard to overcook"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Strip Steak (New York Strip)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Marbling: Good",
        "Tenderness: Tender with slight chew",
        "Thickness: 1-1.5 inches",
        "Why: Balance of flavor and texture, less fatty than ribeye"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Filet Mignon**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Marbling: Minimal",
        "Tenderness: Most tender cut",
        "Thickness: 1.5-2 inches",
        "Why: Melt-in-mouth texture, elegant presentation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://file.notion.so/f/f/b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5/e0497bf3-1ee8-47d1-8023-de0037794e27/vudememe_A_hand-drawn_watercolor-style_illustration_of_a_perfec_4a23e1a6-b58f-4a49-860b-2acfb889355d.png?table=block&id=2f7c3484-e8de-80c2-9317-d1122a4b011a&spaceId=b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5&expirationTimestamp=1774864800000&signature=WBqqQGH0eaUuBecWLW721EQ1CFukV5ISdPxRTxfle8M",
      "caption": null,
      "localPath": "src/assets/images/articles/the-ultimate-guide-to-cooking-a-perfect-steak-for-your-next-date-night.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Quality Indicators"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Look for:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Bright red color (not gray or brown)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Visible marbling (white fat throughout)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Thick cut (minimum 1 inch, preferably 1.5 inches)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Dry surface (not sitting in liquid)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Grade: USDA Prime or Choice"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Avoid:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "❌ Thin steaks (under 1 inch)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "❌ Gray or brown discoloration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "❌ Excessive liquid in package"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "❌ Strong smell"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Essential Preparation Steps"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Step 1: Bring to Room Temperature"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time:** 30-60 minutes before cooking"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Why:** Cold steak cooks unevenly. Room temperature steak develops better crust and cooks more uniformly."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**How:** Remove from fridge, leave on counter loosely covered."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Step 2: Pat Completely Dry"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Why:** Surface moisture creates steam, prevents proper searing."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**How:** Use paper towels to thoroughly dry both sides and edges."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Step 3: Season Generously"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**When:** Just before cooking (or 40 minutes ahead for dry-brining)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**What:** Kosher salt and coarsely ground black pepper"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**How much:** More than you think. About 1/2 teaspoon salt per side for a 1-pound steak."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://file.notion.so/f/f/b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5/0349c148-e764-4e25-b3c8-8c211ae554fa/vudememe_A_hand-drawn_watercolor-style_illustration_of_a_raw_st_59c93e94-60be-4961-9a47-1031bac0c6e7.png?table=block&id=2f7c3484-e8de-80d9-96ab-c9db776b79de&spaceId=b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5&expirationTimestamp=1774864800000&signature=Smoo5ALlZbulQjR-M5Ax4qd-yeU9EKdK2_DNlbjrfhQ",
      "caption": null,
      "localPath": "src/assets/images/articles/the-ultimate-guide-to-cooking-a-perfect-steak-for-your-next-date-night-1.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The Pan-Sear Method (Most Reliable)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Equipment Needed"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Heavy cast iron or stainless steel pan",
        "High smoke point oil (avocado, vegetable)",
        "Instant-read thermometer",
        "Butter, garlic, and fresh herbs (optional finishing)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Steps"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 1: Preheat pan (5 minutes)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Heat pan over high heat until smoking. This is crucial. The pan must be very hot."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 2: Add oil**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Add 1-2 tablespoons high smoke point oil. Swirl to coat."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 3: Add steak**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Lay steak away from you to avoid splatter. Don't move it."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 4: Sear first side (3-4 minutes)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Leave it alone. Resist the urge to peek. A crust is forming."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 5: Flip once**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use tongs. Steak should release easily when ready."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 6: Sear second side (3-4 minutes)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Add butter, garlic, and thyme if desired. Baste with melted butter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 7: Check temperature**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Insert thermometer into thickest part:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Rare: 120-125°F",
        "Medium-rare: 130-135°F",
        "Medium: 135-145°F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 8: Rest (5-10 minutes)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Move to cutting board or plate. Tent loosely with foil. Temperature will rise 5°F during rest."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The Reverse Sear Method (Most Control)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Best for thick steaks (1.5 inches or more) when you want edge-to-edge even cooking."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 1: Preheat oven to 275°F**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 2: Season steak, place on wire rack over baking sheet**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 3: Roast until 10-15°F below target temp (20-40 minutes)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use thermometer to monitor."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 4: Remove and rest (10 minutes)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 5: Sear in screaming hot pan (1 minute per side)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Quick sear for crust without overcooking interior."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Result:** Perfect doneness throughout with excellent crust."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Temperature Guide (Internal Temp)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Rare (120-125°F)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Cool red center",
        "Very soft texture",
        "Maximum juiciness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Medium-Rare (130-135°F) - Recommended"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Warm red center",
        "Tender, juicy",
        "Ideal for most cuts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Medium (135-145°F)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Warm pink center",
        "Slightly firm",
        "Still juicy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Medium-Well (145-155°F)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Mostly gray with hint of pink",
        "Firm texture",
        "Drier"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Well-Done (160°F+)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Gray throughout",
        "Very firm",
        "Significantly drier"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Pro tip:** Always pull steak 5°F below target. It continues cooking while resting."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Common Mistakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Mistake:** Not preheating pan enough"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Solution:** Pan should smoke before steak goes in. This takes 5 full minutes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Mistake:** Moving the steak too much"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Solution:** Let it sit undisturbed to develop crust. Flip only once."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Mistake:** Cutting into it immediately"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Solution:** Rest 5-10 minutes. Juices redistribute, steak stays moist."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Mistake:** Using lean cuts for high heat"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Solution:** Filet mignon needs gentler cooking or butter basting. Ribeye can handle high heat."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Mistake:** Guessing doneness"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Solution:** Use a thermometer. It's the only reliable method."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The Basting Technique"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Adds rich flavor and helps develop crust."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**When:** Last 2 minutes of cooking"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**What:** 2 tablespoons butter, 2 garlic cloves (smashed), 2 sprigs fresh thyme"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**How:** Tilt pan, use spoon to pour melted butter over steak repeatedly (30-40 seconds)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Result:** Enhanced flavor, golden crust, aromatic presentation."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Finishing Touches"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Simple Finishing Options"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "**Flaky sea salt:** Sprinkle on just before serving",
        "**Compound butter:** Slice of herb butter melting on top",
        "**Fresh herbs:** Chopped parsley or chives",
        "**Lemon wedge:** Brightness to cut richness"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Impressive Sauces"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "**Pan sauce:** Deglaze pan with wine, reduce, add butter",
        "**Chimichurri:** Bright, herbaceous, makes ahead",
        "**Béarnaise:** Classic French, rich and elegant",
        "**Blue cheese butter:** Bold flavor for special occasions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Date Night Strategy"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Timing"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Season steaks: 30 minutes before date arrives",
        "Start cooking: When date arrives (impressive to watch)",
        "Rest: While plating sides",
        "Serve: 45 minutes after date arrives"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "The Show"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Cooking steak is theatrical. The sizzle, the butter basting, the aromatic herbs. Position your date where they can watch safely. The confidence you show while cooking is attractive."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "The Result"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A perfectly cooked steak demonstrates competence. When you slice into it and it's exactly the right doneness, that's a moment of validation. You knew what you were doing."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: How do I know when the pan is hot enough?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Hold your hand 6 inches above the pan. If you can't keep it there for more than 2 seconds, it's ready. Or add a drop of water—it should evaporate instantly."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: Should I oil the steak or the pan?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Either works. Oiling the pan is easier and prevents oversaturating the steak."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: My steak always sticks to the pan. Why?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Pan isn't hot enough, or you're moving the steak too soon. When a proper crust forms, it releases naturally."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: Can I cook steak from frozen?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Yes, but it requires the reverse sear method. Add 50% more time to the oven portion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: What if I don't have a thermometer?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The hand test (touching your palm and comparing firmness) works but is less reliable. Invest in an instant-read thermometer."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The Confidence Factor"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Knowing you can cook a perfect steak eliminates date night anxiety. You're not hoping it turns out well, you know it will. This confidence shows in how you carry yourself throughout the evening."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "When your date takes the first bite and you see their reaction, that's validation of your skill. It's a tangible way to demonstrate capability."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "icon": "✓",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Quick Reference Guide:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "ordered",
      "items": [
        "Buy 1.5-inch ribeye or strip steak",
        "Room temp 30 minutes, pat dry",
        "Season generously with salt and pepper",
        "Preheat cast iron 5 minutes until smoking",
        "Sear 3-4 minutes per side",
        "Check temp: pull at 130°F for medium-rare",
        "Rest 5 minutes",
        "Slice and serve"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Practice once before date night."
    }
  ],
